// The descriptor set of the first occlusion-pyramid pass: the depth buffer it reads and the five levels it writes.

// Builds the first five levels of the camera's occlusion-culling pyramid from reversed visibility depth. Each 16x16
// workgroup seeds a block of mip zero, keeps it in workgroup memory, and reduces it in place to one texel of mip
// four, writing every level on the way. Each mip-zero texel keeps the farthest depth, the smallest reversed value, of
// every depth pixel its footprint touches; the pyramid has a fixed extent, so a texel can cover a fraction of a pixel
// or several pixels. The pyramid's extent is a multiple of the block on both axes, so no thread is idle and no write
// needs a bound.
//
// The pyramid stores 16-bit floats. A depth that no 16-bit float holds exactly is rounded toward the far plane, never
// toward the camera, so the pyramid never claims a surface nearer than the one drawn and culling stays conservative.
// Every reduction then takes minimums of 16-bit values, which are exact.
source_depth: descriptor<{ type: Texture2D, binding: 1033, access: read }>;
level_0: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1034, access: write }>;
level_1: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1035, access: write }>;
level_2: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1036, access: write }>;
level_3: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1037, access: write }>;
level_4: descriptor<{ type: StorageImage<r16f>, binding: 1038, access: write }>;
